      },
      {
        "text": "Senator Lummus stated that secret bill drafting is more concerning than 'shadowy super coders' regarding financial innovation.",
        "confidence": 0.92
      },
      {
        "text": "The speaker believes the infrastructure bill may have significant negative consequences for cryptocurrency.",
        "confidence": 0.9
      }
    ],
    "assumptions": [
      {
        "text": "Public scrutiny of legislative processes enhances democratic accountability.",
        "confidence": 0.93
      },
      {
        "text": "Cryptocurrency innovation depends on regulatory transparency and trust in policy-making.",
        "confidence": 0.91
      },
      {
        "text": "The audience values insight into political decisions affecting emerging technologies.",
        "confidence": 0.89
      },
      {
        "text": "The term 'secret bill drafting' implies undemocratic or opaque governance practices.",
        "confidence": 0.88
      },
      {
        "text": "A tweet by a senator constitutes a credible public position on policy matters.",
        "confidence": 0.87
      },
      {
        "text": "Financial innovation is vulnerable to overregulation or lack of clarity in legislation.",
        "confidence": 0.86
      }
    ],
    "turn_type_label": "Substantive",
    "conversation_move_label": "Topic Shift"
  },
  {
    "episode_id": 45973,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/5/45973.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 2,
    "turn_text": "Well, we're trying to improve it. But thus far, I think there have been some negotiations going on between members of the Senate and the Treasury Department that do not adequately reflect the situation on the ground in digital assets. For example, currently it defines broker in a way that could include everyone from Bitcoin miners, people who are putting the blockchain together, people who are custodying peer-to-peer assets, or at least are part of the decentralized effort rather than the centralized effort. It could include too many people under the definition of broker. So we're really trying to narrow that down and get a definition of broker that fits the digital asset space. Too much of this is coming from fiat currency. And as you know, there's not a one to one relationship between the kinds of definitions that are used for fiat currency. and the kinds of definitions that should be used for non-fia currency.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_00",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
      {
        "text": "Efforts are underway to narrow the definition of 'broker'.",
        "confidence": 0.97
      },
      {
        "text": "The current definition of 'broker' applies to too many individuals.",
        "confidence": 0.96
      },
      {
        "text": "The current definition of 'broker' includes Bitcoin miners.",
        "confidence": 0.95
      },
      {
        "text": "A new broker definition should fit the digital asset space.",
        "confidence": 0.95
      },
      {
        "text": "The current definition of 'broker' includes individuals involved in building blockchains.",
        "confidence": 0.94
      },
      {
        "text": "Current regulatory frameworks largely derive from fiat currency models.",
        "confidence": 0.94
      },
      {
        "text": "The current definition of 'broker' includes those responsible for custodying peer-to-peer digital assets.",
        "confidence": 0.93
      },
      {
        "text": "There is no one-to-one correspondence between fiat and non-fiat currency definitions.",
        "confidence": 0.93
      },
      {
        "text": "The current definition of 'broker' may apply to participants in decentralized efforts.",
        "confidence": 0.92
      }
    ],
    "assumptions": [
