    "turn_idx": 33,
    "turn_text": "You know, you should ask him. I'm not sure that it is kosher to share on this podcast anything, but I'd love for you to ask him. Yeah, exactly. Let's see, in terms of, like my question for you is, I've got a lot of sympathy for folks in your position, but, you know, like Jay Powell, I guess I'm, you know, everyone has this argument around inflation where the 50% of the country owns assets in times of inflation, the assets increase in value, so honestly, 50% of the country's gonna make out just fine. The 50% of the country that does know assets is gonna get really, really hurt. It's kind of this simple argument that seems to be quite true. Someone like Jay Powell, is he, Scared like, does he not understand this? Does he genuinely believe that inflation is transitory? Does he genuinely believe you can print massive amounts of money and we won't get inflation? Is he worried about his job and he doesn't want to be the one stuck holding the bag? Like, what is going on here?",
