    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/5/45973.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 38,
    "turn_text": "I think it's a concern about the regulatory environment as opposed to the statutory environment. It's hard to tell where the regulators are being cautious about it and where they're being aggressive. It looks to me like Treasury is being very aggressive in a negative way towards cryptocurrency. So we all need to keep our eye on Treasury and try to work with them. But they're in a unique position. So while I've been trying to work with the SEC with the Fed, with the FDIC, with the CFDC, the treasury seems to be the one that is flexing their muscles the most in a negative way. And I think that's the biggest concern right now, is to get regulators to back off and take a deep breath and let us all work through this in a very open and transparent forum. So somebody's not behind the scenes like Treasury's doing right now, apparently, trying to upend these discussions at a time when they can really do a lot of damage to innovation.",
