    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/5/45973.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 40,
    "turn_text": "That's a great question. You know, some people are surprising me. Marsha Blackburn knows a lot more about it than I first was aware of. There are senators who have asked for books that I have and said, hey, send me a copy of that book. One of those is Tom Tillis. I think that he's one of those people who just genuinely doesn't know anything about it and chose to read about it. So I think you're going to see from people who are inquisitive, just intellectually inquisitive, that they're going to come along and want to be part of things. I think John Hickenlooper from Colorado, is someone who will take an interest in this in a bigger way. Of course, Kirsten Sinema, she's super smart. She graduated from college when she was 18 years old. And this is someone who came out of a very, very rough family background and tough financial background as a kid. So she's a very uniquely smart person. But there are a lot of people like that in the Senate. So the goal here, is to get to know them. Pat Toomey surprised me when he released his financial reports, and we found",
